WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
TurnBased · AI-assisted game design
Give the AI agent a game idea. Let it write your rulebook.

2
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:19.120
1. Describe the game
Players, actions, scoring, and the constraints you want to keep.

3
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:24.480
2. The AI agent writes the rules
A real AI request drafts five chapters. Generation wait shortened.

4
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.000
3. Review what the AI wrote
Five connected chapters. Your original rules stay unchanged until you apply.

5
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.120
AI draft · Setup
The agent specifies the components, starting resources, and shared market.

6
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:41.920
AI draft · Taking a Turn
It writes the legal actions and a worked example, using your constraints.

7
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:47.360
AI draft · End Game
Victory conditions and tie handling are part of the same draft.

8
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:55.280
4. Apply the rules you approve
One click adds all five AI-written chapters. Every line remains editable.

9
00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:04.320
5. Design the pieces that go with it
Reuse one editable template across your prepared card table.

10
00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:12.320
6. Try your deck in the playtest lab
A supported market-race simulation uses your card costs and points.

11
00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:19.600
7. Export the prototype
Download the AI-written rulebook and print your component designs.

12
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.120
TurnBased · turnbased.app
Your game idea. AI-written rules. A prototype you can keep improving.
